# Generate RS256 keypair — required before running the server
mkdir server\keys
# Run this in WSL or Git Bash (openssl):
openssl genrsa -out server/keys/private.pem 2048
openssl rsa -in server/keys/private.pem -pubout -out server/keys/public.pem

# Then copy .env.example → .env and fill in your OAuth credentials
cp .env.example .env



## To run locally right now

**Step 1 — Generate keys** (run in Git Bash / WSL)
```bash
mkdir server/keys
openssl genrsa -out server/keys/private.pem 2048
openssl rsa -in server/keys/private.pem -pubout -out server/keys/public.pem
```

**Step 2 — Create `.env`**
```bash
cp server/.env.local.example server/.env
# Fill in GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET, GITHUB_CLIENT_ID, GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET
```

**Step 3 — OAuth app settings** (important: update redirect URIs)
- Google Cloud Console → your OAuth app → add `http://localhost:3001/oauth/callback/google`
- GitHub → your OAuth app → callback URL: `http://localhost:3001/oauth/callback/github`

**Step 4 — Start Postgres + Redis**
```bash
docker compose up postgres redis -d
```

**Step 5 — Run the server**
```bash
cd server && air   # or: go run ./cmd/main.go
```

**Step 6 — Verify**
```
GET http://localhost:3001/health
GET http://localhost:3001/.well-known/jwks.json
```

